\label{def:sau-transfer-plan}
An \emph{SAU transfer plan} from a source package \(\mathfrak C_s\) to a target package \(\mathfrak C_t\) is a triple
\[
\operatorname{Transfer}(\mathfrak C_s,\mathfrak C_t;\mathfrak p)
\]
such that:
\begin{enumerate}
\item \(\Inst_{\mathsf{SAU}}(\mathfrak p,\mathfrak C_s)\), so the source realizes \(\mathfrak p\) with a validated certificate;
\item \(\operatorname{Inst}(\mathfrak p,\mathfrak C_t)\), so the target inhabits the same profile skeleton;
\item the target has its own candidate witness fields and instruments, not merely borrowed source witnesses.
\end{enumerate}
The transfer plan is \emph{validated} when additionally
\[
\mathbf F_{\mathsf{SAU}}(\mathfrak C_t)=\varnothing.
\]

